 ## Background
-The method was introduced in the context of real-time super-resolution contextual close-up of clinical volumetric data [S1]. It addresses the need for fast silhouette extraction and shading in direct volume rendering, where gradient calculations are expensive. The technique leverages the properties of B-spline subdivision, which preserves vector normalization, allowing gradients to be quantized without repeated normalization costs [S1].
